{
  "sutta_id": "SN43.44",
  "verses": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "pali": "Saṁyutta Nikāya 43.44 ",
      "english": "Linked Discourses 43.44 "
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "pali": "2. Dutiyavagga ",
      "english": "Chapter Two "
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "pali": "Parāyanasutta ",
      "english": "The Final Haven "
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "pali": "“Parāyanañca vo, bhikkhave, desessāmi parāyanagāmiñca maggaṁ. ",
      "english": "“Mendicants, I will teach you the final haven and the path that leads to the final haven. "
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "pali": "Taṁ suṇātha. ",
      "english": "Listen … "
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "pali": "Katamañca, bhikkhave, parāyanaṁ? ",
      "english": "And what is the final haven? "
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "pali": "Yo, bhikkhave, rāgakkhayo dosakkhayo mohakkhayo—",
      "english": "The ending of greed, hate, and delusion. "
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "pali": "idaṁ vuccati, bhikkhave, parāyanaṁ. ",
      "english": "This is called the final haven. "
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "pali": "Katamo ca, bhikkhave, parāyanagāmī maggo? ",
      "english": "And what is the path that leads to the final haven? "
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "pali": "Kāyagatāsati. ",
      "english": "Mindfulness of the body. "
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "pali": "Ayaṁ vuccati, bhikkhave, parāyanagāmimaggo. ",
      "english": "This is called the path that leads to the final haven. "
    },
    {
      "number": 12,
      "pali": "Iti kho, bhikkhave, desitaṁ vo mayā parāyanaṁ, desito parāyanagāmimaggo. ",
      "english": "So, mendicants, I’ve taught you the final haven and the path that leads to the final haven. "
    },
    {
      "number": 13,
      "pali": "Yaṁ, bhikkhave, satthārā karaṇīyaṁ sāvakānaṁ hitesinā anukampakena anukampaṁ upādāya, kataṁ vo taṁ mayā. ",
      "english": "Out of sympathy, I’ve done what a teacher should do who wants what’s best for their disciples. "
    },
    {
      "number": 14,
      "pali": "Etāni, bhikkhave, rukkhamūlāni, etāni suññāgārāni. Jhāyatha, bhikkhave, mā pamādattha; mā pacchā vippaṭisārino ahuvattha. Ayaṁ vo amhākaṁ anusāsanī”ti. ",
      "english": "Here are these roots of trees, and here are these empty huts. Practice absorption, mendicants! Don’t be negligent! Don’t regret it later! This is my instruction to you.” "
    },
    {
      "number": 15,
      "pali": "(Yathā asaṅkhataṁ tathā vitthāretabbaṁ.) ",
      "english": "(Tell in full as in the unconditioned.) "
    },
    {
      "number": 16,
      "pali": "Tettiṁsatimaṁ. ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 17,
      "pali": "Dutiyo vaggo. ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 18,
      "pali": "Tassuddānaṁ ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 19,
      "pali": "Asaṅkhataṁ anataṁ anāsavaṁ, ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 20,
      "pali": "Saccañca pāraṁ nipuṇaṁ sududdasaṁ; ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 21,
      "pali": "Ajajjaraṁ dhuvaṁ apalokitaṁ, ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 22,
      "pali": "Anidassanaṁ nippapañca santaṁ. ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 23,
      "pali": "Amataṁ paṇītañca sivañca khemaṁ, ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 24,
      "pali": "Taṇhākkhayo acchariyañca abbhutaṁ; ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 25,
      "pali": "Anītikaṁ anītikadhammaṁ, ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 26,
      "pali": "Nibbānametaṁ sugatena desitaṁ. ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 27,
      "pali": "Abyābajjho virāgo ca, ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 28,
      "pali": "suddhi mutti anālayo; ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 29,
      "pali": "Dīpo leṇañca tāṇañca, ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 30,
      "pali": "saraṇañca parāyananti. ",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "number": 31,
      "pali": "Asaṅkhatasaṁyuttaṁ samattaṁ. ",
      "english": "The Linked Discourses on the unconditioned are complete. "
    }
  ]
}